The natural inclusion $L\hookrightarrow R$ induces, for every compact profinite $T$, a quasi-isomorphism $$\label{eq:ordinary-perfect-P-comparison}
 C^\bullet_{\mathrm{cts}}(P,L;T)\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }C^\bullet_{\mathrm{cts}}(P,R;T).$$ It is $J$-equivariant and natural in $T$. With discrete cohomology groups, evaluation gives $$\label{eq:ordinary-four-rows}
 H^aC^\bullet_{\mathrm{cts}}(P,L;T)=
 \begin{cases}
 C_{\mathrm{cts}}(T,k),&a=0,1,\\
 C_{\mathrm{cts}}(T,\ell),&a=3,4,\\
 0,&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}$$ Here the identifications in degrees one and four use the same nonzero element of $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}_{\mathrm{cts}}(1+3\mathbb Z_3,\mathbb F_p)$. The $J$-action is trivial in degrees zero and one. On each upper line, its restriction to $\mathcal O_F^\times$ is the nontrivial norm character $\delta$.

The natural augmentation induces an equivalence $$\label{eq:tested-totalization}
  Y/p\simeq\mathop{\mathrm{Tot}}\mathcal T(C^\bullet).$$ The corresponding spectral sequence $$\label{eq:tested-spectral-sequence}
  \mathsf E_2^{s,t}
     =H^s\bigl(\pi_t\mathcal T(C^\bullet)\bigr)
       \Longrightarrow\pi_{t-s}(Y/p)$$ is strongly convergent, with a horizontal vanishing line at a finite page and a finite filtration on its abutment. Its differentials are $k[[x]]$-linear and $J$-semilinear-equivariant.*

*There is a compatible diagonal summand, denoted by a subscript $\Delta$, on every page and on the abutment filtration: it is the summand on which the two copies of $k$, from $E_2$ and $S_k$, agree. The same assertions hold on that summand.

The ordinary, unlocalized smash product has even homotopy and $$\label{eq:ordinary-kunneth}
  \pi_*(E_2\wedge C^s)
    =(E_2)_*(E_3)\otimes_{E_{3*}}
          \operatorname{Map}_{\mathrm{cts}}(P^s,E_{3*}).$$ This module is flat over $E_{2*}$. In particular, $D_m^s$ is flat over $A_m$, and reduction by $(p,x^m)$ creates no odd homotopy. There are natural identifications $$\label{eq:residue-cochains}
  D_1^s=
  \operatorname{Map}_{\mathrm{cts}}(P^s,K)\otimes_K L
    =\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}_U\operatorname{Map}_{\mathrm{cts}}(P^s,L^U),$$ compatible with the bar maps and the marking actions.

The diagonal homotopy cochains of $\mathcal T(C^\bullet)$ are zero in odd internal degrees. In degree $2j$ they are naturally $$\label{eq:completed-homotopy-cochains}
  \left(\lim_m D_m^\bullet\right)
             \otimes_{k[[x]]}\Omega^{\otimes j}.$$ The maps to the finite quotients on homotopy groups are the ordinary reduction maps.

The diagonal spectral sequence of Proposition <a href="#prop:descent-test" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:descent-test">44</a>, after extension of scalars to $Q_x$, collapses at its second page. For every $r\in\mathbb Z$, its actual abutment filtration gives $G_F$-equivariant short exact sequences $$\begin{aligned}
 0&\longrightarrow
 Q_x(\delta)\otimes_{Q_x}\overline\omega^{\otimes(r+2)}
 \longrightarrow\mathcal V_{2r}^\Delta(Z_k)
 \longrightarrow\overline\omega^{\otimes r}\longrightarrow0,
 \label{eq:generic-even-filtration}\\
 0&\longrightarrow
 Q_x(\delta)\otimes_{Q_x}\overline\omega^{\otimes(r+1)}
 \longrightarrow\mathcal V_{2r-1}^\Delta(Z_k)
 \longrightarrow\overline\omega^{\otimes r}\longrightarrow0.
 \label{eq:generic-odd-filtration}
\end{aligned}$$ In particular, each diagonal summand $\mathcal V_d^\Delta(Z_k)$ has dimension two over $Q_x$, and $\mathcal V_{-3}^\Delta(Z_k)$ contains a subrepresentation isomorphic to $Q_x(\delta)$.

