There is a finite étale $S$-algebra $S_k$ with $\pi_0S_k=W(k)$. If $d=[k:\mathbb F_p]$, then $$\label{eq:spherical-constants}
  \pi_*S_k=\pi_*S\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}W(k),\qquad
  S_k\simeq S^{\oplus d}
  \quad\text{as $S$-modules}.$$ The coefficient inclusions give canonical maps $S_k\to E_i(k)$, and stabilizer automorphisms fixing $k$ are $S_k$-linear. Set $$\label{eq:test-spectra}
  Z_k=L_{K(3)}S_k,\qquad
  Y=L_{K(2)}(E_2\wedge Z_k).$$ The algebra $E_3(k)$ is descendable over $Z_k$ in the $K(3)$-local category. For its Amitsur object $$\label{eq:morava-amitsur}
  C^s=\underbrace{E_3\otimes^{K(3)}_{Z_k}\cdots
                    \otimes^{K(3)}_{Z_k}E_3}_{s+1\text{ factors}},$$ completed Morava cooperations identify $$\label{eq:unextended-cooperations}
  \pi_*C^s=\operatorname{Map}_{\mathrm{cts}}(P^s,E_{3*}),$$ with the adic coefficient topology and the usual evaluation and stabilizer-action faces.

